{"chapter": 4, "sha256": "1386133327689f27f9cbdbceb53ab9b496a623a497a17930552354a217b341e9", "voice": {"voice_id": "ppLqTilh7rH7fbUVlXsf", "name": "David - Documentary", "model_id": "eleven_v3", "voice_settings": {"stability": 0.5, "similarity_boost": 0.8, "style": 0.0, "use_speaker_boost": true}}, "source": "docs/script.md", "files": {"narration": {"file": "ch4.mp3", "text": "A papyrus in Turin, copied about 1250 BCE, lists kings back to Menes, and before him gods, spirits and Followers of Horus. On its most probable reading, the spirits and Followers get 13,420 years and, in the next line, 23,200. The papyrus is some 1,850 years younger than Menes, and partly restored.\n\nThe Egyptians called that beginning sep tepi, the First Time. Hancock and Bauval read it as memory, not myth.\n\nA stela by the Great Pyramid has Khufu finding a house of Isis \"beside the house of the Sphinx\". So, they argue, the Sphinx predates Khafre. Its translator, James Breasted, called the evidence for a late date \"entirely conclusive.\"\n\nIn King Unas's tomb, about 2400 BCE, the oldest Pyramid Texts say \"Unas appears as a star\" and \"Orion is encircled by the Duat,\" with Sothis, our Sirius, and Unas.\n\nNone of these texts gives a date. Hancock and Bauval look for one in the sky.", "seconds": 98.8, "alignment": {"characters": ["A", " ", "p", "a", "p", "y", "r", "u", "s", " ", "i", "n", " ", "T", "u", "r", "i", "n", ",", " ", "c", "o", "p", "i", "e", "d", " ", "a", "b", "o", "u", "t", " ", "1", "2", "5", "0", " ", "B", "C", "E", ",", " ", "l", "i", "s", "t", "s", " ", "k", "i", "n", "g", "s", " ", "b", "a", "c", "k", " ", "t", "o", " ", "M", "e", "n", "e", "s", ",", " ", "a", "n", "d", " ", "b", "e", "f", "o", "r", "e", " ", "h", "i", "m", " ", "g", "o", "d", "s", ",", " ", "s", "p", "i", "r", "i", "t", "s", " ", "a", "n", "d", " ", "F", "o", "l", "l", "o", "w", "e", "r", "s", " ", "o", "f", " ", "H", "o", "r", "u", "s", ".", " ", "O", "n", " ", "i", "t", "s", " ", "m", "o", "s", "t"